  "title": "Whose is this?",
  "goal": "Ask whose something is with kimiň and who has it with kimde, and follow a short talk about lost things.",
  "points": ["gp-whose", "gp-genitive-possessive", "gp-pronominal-n"],
  "intro": {
    "text": "**Whose?** is *kimiň?*, and the thing takes **his** or **her**: *Bu kimiň sagady?* (Whose watch is this?) **Who has it?** is *kimde?*: *Açar kimde? — Mende.* To hand something over, say *Ine*.",
    "see": "gp-whose"
  },
  "vocab": [
    { "tk": "kimiň", "en": "whose", "pos": "pron" },
    { "tk": "kimde", "en": "who has it? (literally on whom)", "pos": "pron" },
    { "tk": "ine", "en": "here (it is); look", "pos": "interj", "card": "fc-0101" },
    { "tk": "ýer", "en": "place; seat", "pos": "noun", "card": "fc-0057" },
    { "tk": "başga", "en": "other, another; different", "pos": "adj", "card": "fc-0086" }
  ],
  "exercises": [
    {
      "id": "a1-u10-l04-e01",
      "type": "mcq",
      "points": ["gp-whose"],
      "question": "How do you ask **whose**?",
      "options": ["kimiň", "kimde", "kime", "kimi"],
      "optionsLang": "tk",
      "answer": 0,
      "why": {
        "1": "*kimde* asks **who has it**.",
        "2": "*kime* is **to whom**.",
        "3": "*kimi* is **whom**, as an object."
      },
      "explain": "*kim* + the genitive *-iň* = *kimiň*, whose."
    },
    {
